  "release_delivery_days": 7,
  "release_notes_md": "v0.1.3 closes the v0.1.2 transient race window.\n\nv0.1.2 used `pg_try_advisory_xact_lock` + early return for the migration loser worker, but that loser then started its background services BEFORE the winner's migration transaction committed \u2014 producing a ~5s window of transient `UndefinedTable` errors in service logs + a single HTTP 500 on the first dashboard load.\n\n**Fix (api `d330fbf` develop)**: switch to blocking `pg_advisory_xact_lock`. Loser waits for winner's COMMIT (which releases the xact-lock) before proceeding. By the time it starts services, schema is committed and visible. No more transient first-tick window.\n\nOther repos in this release are no-op tag bumps. Recommended for any v0.1.2 fresh install that observed transient errors at boot. Same compatibility envelope as v0.1.2 (`from: v0.1.0`).",
  "released_at": "2026-05-17T04:18:27Z",
